摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Package manager for AI agent assets — 42 skills, 5 CLIs, 1 plugin. Skills for AI/LLM agent engineering, eval-driven dev, spec-driven dev, database (MySQL/PG/Redis/Kafka/Mongo/Oracle/NL2SQL), K8s/Docker diagnostics, infra ops (Dify/Nexus/Harbor/SonarQube) & docs/patent. Runtimes: ","id":"gh:1324754350","install_available":false,"language":"Python","name":"harness-ai-kit","slug":"seed-forge/harness-ai-kit","topics":["agent-framework","agent-skills","ai-agents","claude-code","claude-skills","codex","cursor","database","dify","docker","dsh","dsh-plugin","kiro","kubernetes","llm","mcp","mysql","nexus","python","sonarqube"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Package manager for AI agent assets — 42 skills, 5 CLIs, 1 plugin. Skills for AI/LLM agent engineeri"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"ng, eval-driven dev, spec-driven dev, database (MySQL/PG/Redis/Kafka/Mongo/Oracle/NL2SQL), K8s/Docke"},{"id":"p1s3","text":"r diagnostics, infra ops (Dify/Nexus/Harbor/SonarQube) & docs/patent. Runtimes: "},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# harness-ai-kit"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**A package manager and composition layer for AI agent assets.**"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"`harness-ai-kit` installs, resolves, locks, validates, and synchronizes Skills,\nCLIs, MCPs, plugins,"},{"id":"p4s2","text":" hooks, subagents, and loops across Codex, Claude Code,\nCursor, Kiro, and DeepSeek Harness (dsh)."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Quickstart · Asset Catalog · Usage Scenarios · Concepts · Roadmap · Changelog · 中文文档"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Why"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"AI teams collect useful prompts, Skills, CLIs, and MCP servers quickly. The\nhard part is making that"},{"id":"p7s2","text":" collection reproducible: knowing what is installed,\nwhich versions work together, where it is mater"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"ialized, and how a teammate can\nget the same working state without copying runtime directories."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"`harness-ai-kit` makes the project manifest the source of truth:"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"The lock records resolved sources and checksums. Installation uses a staging\ndirectory and only repl"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"aces the runtime target after the selected assets are\nready. The result is useful for one developer,"},{"id":"p10s3","text":" and essential when a team needs\nthe same AI engineering environment across projects and runtimes."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## The REMIX Method"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"This project is a composition layer, not another vertical AI toolkit. When a\nfocused community Skill"},{"id":"p12s2","text":", CLI, or MCP already solves a problem, the preferred\npath is to compose it, pin it, and make it rep"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"roducible instead of rebuilding\nit."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"- **R**euse proven assets from the community or your own repositories.\n- **E**xtend an asset when a "},{"id":"p13s2","text":"small, explicit adaptation is enough.\n- **M**ix Skills, CLIs, MCPs, and runtime assets into one work"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"flow.\n- **I**ntegrate the selected assets through a typed manifest and lockfile.\n- e**X**ecute the s"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"ame declared environment across supported runtimes."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## No Lock-In"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"An installed Skill is still a normal directory of Markdown and metadata. You\ncan read it, copy it, o"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"r install it directly from its Git repository without\nusing this tool. `harness-ai-kit` is not a gat"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"ekeeper for content; it adds the\nreproducible inventory, dependency resolution, checksums, and runti"},{"id":"p15s4","text":"me sync\naround that content."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"## Quick Start"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Requirements: Python 3.10+ and Git."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"`init` creates or updates the shared configuration at\n`~/.harness-ai-kit/config.yaml`. `init-project"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"` creates the project manifest;\n`sync` resolves it, writes the lockfile, and materializes the select"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"ed assets\nfor the configured runtime. See the quickstart for\nruntime-specific installation details."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## Team Workflow"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Commit the declaration and lockfile, not copied runtime directories:"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"This keeps local customizations out of version control while allowing a shared,\nauditable AI asset b"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"aseline. `sync` reconciles managed assets; it is not a\nblind wipe of unrelated local files."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"## What It Provides"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"| Capability | Outcome |"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"| Typed asset model | One dependency contract for Skills, CLIs, MCPs, plugins, hooks, subagents, and"},{"id":"p26s2","text":" loops |\n| Resolution and lockfiles | A reproducible selection of versions, sources, features, and S"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"HA-256 checksums |\n| Multiple runtime adapters | Project or global installation for supported AI cod"},{"id":"p26s4","text":"ing runtimes |\n| Git-based sources | Install a reviewed Skill directly from a public Git repository "},{"id":"p26s5","text":"|\n| Safe materialization | Staging, verification, replacement, and rollback-aware installation flow "},{"id":"p26s6","text":"|\n| Configuration boundary | User-specific endpoints and credentials live in `~/.harness-ai-kit/conf"},{"id":"p26s7","text":"ig.yaml`, not in assets |\n| Curated public assets | Reusable engineering, diagnostic, and AI-develop"},{"id":"p26s8","text":"ment assets listed in the catalog |"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## Architecture"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"The public project deliberately separates portable product behavior from\nprivate operating context. "},{"id":"p29s2","text":"Public packages must work with a user's own\nconfiguration and public dependencies; private endpoints"},{"id":"p29s3","text":", credentials, and\ndeployment topology do not belong in the published tree."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"## Usage Paths"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"- **Adopt a public Skill:** install from a Git repository, then sync it into a\nproject runtime.\n- **"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"Share an engineering baseline:** commit the manifest and lockfile so the\nteam resolves the same asse"},{"id":"p31s3","text":"ts.\n- **Author an internal or public asset:** use the metadata contract, validate\nit locally, and pu"},{"id":"p31s4","text":"blish only through an explicit reviewed release path.\n- **Run dsh:** install Skills or the bundled p"},{"id":"p31s5","text":"lugin through the dsh runtime\nadapter. See dsh integration."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"The usage scenarios explain when to use a Skill,\nwhen a loop is appropriate, and how a spec-driven w"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"orkflow can route both."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"## Roadmap"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"The current public product focuses on portable asset management, reproducible\ninstallation, and a re"},{"id":"p34s2","text":"viewed public catalog. Future work expands authoring and\nautomation first; registry, browser, and or"},{"id":"p34s3","text":"ganization administration remain\nseparate platform milestones rather than hidden dependencies of the"},{"id":"p34s4","text":" administration remain\nseparate platform milestones rather than hidden dependencies of the core CLI."},{"id":"p35s1","text":"See ROADMAP.md for scope, milestones, and non-goals."},{"id":"p36s1","text":"## Documentation"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"- Quickstart\n- Core concepts\n- CLI reference\n- Asset catalog\n- Asset authoring contract\n- Troublesho"},{"id":"p37s2","text":"oting\n- OSS release process"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"## Contributing And Security"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"Use CONTRIBUTING.md for contribution expectations and\nSECURITY.md for responsible disclosure. Issues"},{"id":"p39s2","text":" and feature\nrequests belong in the GitHub issue tracker; open-ended design discussion can\nuse GitHu"},{"id":"p39s3","text":"equests belong in the GitHub issue tracker; open-ended design discussion can\nuse GitHub Discussions."},{"id":"p40s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"Apache-2.0 © 2026 SeedForge."}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
